{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And you shall take possession</b> — two times: here and the other concerning a slave, which is likened to land." "<b>And you shall take possession</b> — inheritance appears four times in the verse, each alef having a value of four: in the mountain, in the plain, in the lowland, and on the seacoast. The verse begins and ends with נחלה, to teach that in the place where the lot fell, even if far from one another, one may not change."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:44.563289106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}